Qt-derived Unicode bidi resolver for LibreCAD
=============================================

Upstream: Qt qtbase, src/gui/text/qtextengine.cpp, QBidiAlgorithm
Version: v6.11.2
Commit: ef55f427f2c8b410d34f8a7681020a3000cf6866
Source: https://github.com/qt/qtbase/blob/ef55f427f2c8b410d34f8a7681020a3000cf6866/src/gui/text/qtextengine.cpp
Upstream source SHA-256:
a6eb23e84fed66f80e4ca3274f413d7a686e1e54b405b97f1cd3f53e215096eb

Qt copyright and SPDX notices are retained. The Qt-derived code is used
under Qt's GPL-2.0-only option; LibreCAD modifications and integration
files are GPL-2.0-or-later. The GPL version 2 text is in
../../licenses/gpl-2.0.txt.

This is a source extraction, not a call to Qt's private ABI. It requires
only public QtCore APIs, C++17, and no GUI application or font database.
Qt supplies Unicode properties; the supported Unicode version follows
the Qt runtime.

Local changes:
- Replace private QScriptAnalysis and QUnicodeTables with a small local
  analysis record and public QChar property queries.
- Decode supplementary characters in the bidi fast-path check and
  propagate X9/L1 properties to both UTF-16 units of boundary neutrals.
- Resolve NSMs after either paired bracket, skipping X9-removed controls
  within the isolating run sequence.
- Scan bracket contents only within their isolating run sequence, and
  count a PDI in the run it resumes rather than the run it closes.
- Keep X9-removed embedding/override controls neutral to weak-type
  resolution, including when a directional override is active.
- Preserve run continuation across empty embeddings before an isolate,
  and match all FSI/PDI pairs even beyond the explicit-level depth limit.
- Match canonical bracket equivalents through Qt normalization, without
  conflating compatibility forms or maintaining a bracket table.
- Provide bounded UTF-16 embedding levels and an L2 visual index map.

Paragraph separation and LFF grapheme handling belong to lc_textbidi.
Glyph metrics and geometry belong to RS_Text/RS_MText. This resolver does
not perform Arabic contextual shaping or OpenType glyph substitution.

Validation uses Unicode 17 BidiTest.txt and BidiCharacterTest.txt:
770241 type/direction cases and 91707 character cases. These validate
paragraph levels and L2 maps; they do not cover LFF glyph geometry,
shaping, or line wrapping. Run the small committed regressions for the
normal incremental development loop, and the external Unicode corpora
when changing the resolver or updating its upstream version.

With BUILD_TESTS=ON, build the opt-in librecad_bidi_conformance target,
then run it with paths to the official BidiTest.txt and
BidiCharacterTest.txt for the Qt runtime's Unicode version. Corpus files
are external inputs and are not bundled. The runner needs only QtCore.
